The Last of Us HBO's new zombie drama is  based on the unforgettable game but how  do the characters stack up between the  show and the source material  fans of the video game are bound to have  a closer relationship with Joe Miller  than any other character in the series  not only is he the protagonist of the  story but he is also the character  controlled by the player for the  majority of the game Pedro Pascal plays  Joel in the television series while the  character was voiced by Troy Baker in  the game pass guard has proven himself  more than capable of helming a  television series for starring roles in  the Mandalorian and narcos the only  notable cosmetic change in Joel is an  ethnic shift away from the game's  Caucasian iteration of Joel to suit  Pascal's Chilean Heritage this switch is  unlikely to have any effect on the  narrative and falls in line with Neil's  drug min's commendable focus on  increasing diversity whenever possible  which was reflected in The Last of Us  Part 2 when speaking with GQ druckman  said that he considers a diverse cast of  characters to be as important as any  other storytelling or gameplay  components based on everything we've  seen thus far Pascal seems to have  nailed Joel's Gruff nature and rugged  mannerisms and judging from its own face  your hair down to the broken watch that  serves as a reminder of his daughter  Sarah's death he looks the part I'm not  family no  cargo  alongside Joel Ellie Williams as the  other main character and the only other  person that players control for portions  of the game aside from Sarah for a brief  time in the prologue Ellie is played by  Bella Ramsay in the HBO show while she  was voiced by Ashley Johnson in the  games Ramsay is still early on in her  career and is best known for her  portrayal of Leona Mormont on HBO's Game  of Thrones which provided her with her  very first role she has had a few  notable roles since such as a recurring  character on his dark materials but the  last of us has set to become her biggest  starring role to date although Ramsay is  19 years old which is five years older  than Ellie is in the game she has a  youthful enough appearance surpassed for  a 14 year old and more or less matches  the look and height of the video game  character Ramsay looks the part right  down to the eyebrow scar but the one  noteworthy visual change from the game  is Ramsey's brunette hair color Ali's  hair in the game is Auburn the character  is also referred to in dialogue as a  redhead in the game Ellie's hair color  had already been a point of confusion  amongst fans of the game and the TV  series will likely exacerbate that  debate  set is an important character early on  in the story of the last of us though  she does not continue with Ellie and  Joel on their cross-country Adventure  she has both a close personal and  professional relationship with Joel and  she is the one who convinces him to  transport Ali to Salt Lake City from  Boston to get to the fireflies in the TV  series Tess is played by anatov who is  best known for her roles on the show's  mind Hunter and Fringe tour was no  stranger to video games having earlier  provided the voice of the main character  in Heavenly sword visually 12 seems to  capture Tess's toughness and to make up  matches Tessa's injuries quite well in  the show cesus has seems considerably  longer and she's lacking the trademark  black and white bandana that holds her  hair up in the game the red shirt worn  by Tess and the game seems to be present  but it's covered by an outer layer  overall it doesn't seem like the show's  version of Tess will be a major  departure from her depiction in the game  in the game bill is a memorable side  character voiced by W Earl Brown who  only appears in the Lincoln chapter  casting a household name like Nick  Offerman in the role and including him  in four episodes instead of just one  suggests that the series will expand on  this portion of the original story a  casting of Murray Barlett as Frank in  four episodes furthers his implication  in the game Frank is dead by the time  players find him but his backstory  subtly reveals him to be Bill's former  romantic partner Offerman seems like the  perfect casting for Bill the video game  version of Bill is a bit more out of  shape and generally and camps on the TV  version appears to be but offer money  said a decent fit for Bill's physicality  and a great match for its personality  and demeanor cosmetically offerman's  beard is darker and a bit Fuller than  video game bills and his hair is a bit  tidier but the style isn't far off  modeling is a key figure amongst the  fireflies a paramilitary resistance  group with questionable morals in the  game she has present in Boston and after  being wounded leaves Ellie in the care  of Joel and Tess she later re-emerges  near the end of the story when the  protagonist finally reached the Firefly  base in Salt Lake City in both the video  game and the HBO series Marlene is  played by Merle Dandridge while there  are a handful of voice actors from the  game contributing live-action  performances in the TV series dandrich  is the only actor to play the same  character across both mediums the  casting couldn't possibly get any more  authentic than this her voice is  guaranteed to be 100 accurate to the  game and although the game's character  design wasn't explicitly modeled after  her she also looks to pass her wardrobe  and hair seemed to be a perfect match  for the character model as well  inclusion of Riley makes it clear that  the HBO series isn't just adapting the  base version of The Last of Us it's  tackling the Left Behind DLC as well  Riley is mentioned through dialogue in  the game but doesn't appear until the  prequel DLC Ellie and Riley are close  friends and begin to form a romance  until disaster strikes I haven't seen  you  and I don't even know how long  45 days  they are both bitten by the infected at  the same time leading to Riley's death  and the discovery that Ellie is immune  to the cordyceps infection in Left  Behind Riley was voiced by Yani King  monshine who was in her 40s in real life  since the character is meant to be 16 in  the game a younger actor was needed for  the live-action adaptation storm Reed  who's the same age as co-star beta  Ramsey takes over as Riley in the show  in terms of costuming the TV version of  Riley has added a head wrapping to hold  her head back that wasn't present in the  game she also wears her hair in a long  ponytail whereas the game character  keeps the hair in a tight burn a  wardrobe has longer sleeves than the  game equivalent but otherwise lines up  well even down to the beaded bracelet on  her wrist  Tommy Miller is Joel's brother and is a  major character in both the last of us  and The Last of Us Part 2. just like  Joel Tommy is Caucasian in the video  game but he's got another ethnicity in  the TV show and a spirit of diversity  and to line up with leading man Pedro  Pascal in the show Tommy is played by  Gabrielle Luna who's of Mexican descent  in the video game The Brothers don't  reunite until far into Joel and Ellie's  cross-country Journey Tommy is slated to  appear in all 10 episodes in the first  season it's clear that Tommy will be a  substantially larger character in the  show than he was in the first game  visually Tommy looks quite different  between the mediums Luna Sports a  different hair color and style he has  clean shaven as opposed to sporting a  full beard as he does in the game also  he is free from the scars and blemishes  present on his digital counterparts  though that might change as a series  progresses his wardrobe is a direct  match for the Tommy of the game with a  fluffy colored jean jacket and it can be  seen using a sniper rifle which is  revealed to be a specialty of Tommy's in  The Last of Us Part 2.  Sarah Miller is Joel's daughter who  meets a heartbreaking end in the opening  moments of the game as 